# Goal-to-Feature decomposition prompt — turns a Goal into FeatureSpecs.

# auto-heal goal decomposition

Given a project goal and current state, propose **independently actionable**
new feature requests that move the project closer to the goal. Do not edit
code; this is a planning pass only.

## Goal: {{ goal.name }}
{% if goal.description -%}
{{ goal.description }}

{% endif -%}
{% if goal.kpis -%}
**KPIs**
{% for kpi in goal.kpis -%}
- `{{ kpi.name }}` — target {{ kpi.target }} (direction: {{ kpi.direction }}{% if kpi.unit %}, unit: {{ kpi.unit }}{% endif %})
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{% if goal.deadline -%}
**Deadline**: {{ goal.deadline }}
{%- endif %}

{% if kpi_status -%}
## Current KPI status
{{ kpi_status }}

{% endif -%}
{% if recent_snapshots -%}
## Recent KPI snapshots (last 30 days)
{{ recent_snapshots }}

{% endif -%}
{% if open_features -%}
## Open feature requests (avoid duplicating these)
{% for fr in open_features -%}
- #{{ fr.id }} [{{ fr.status }}] {{ fr.title }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}

## Repository overview
- Default branch: `{{ repo_state.default_branch }}`
{% if repo_state.languages -%}
- Languages: {{ repo_state.languages | join(", ") }}
{%- endif %}
{% if repo_state.top_level_paths -%}
- Top-level: {{ repo_state.top_level_paths | join(", ") }}
{%- endif %}
{% if repo_state.recent_commits -%}
- Recent commits:
{% for line in repo_state.recent_commits -%}
  - {{ line }}
{% endfor -%}
{%- endif %}

## Output (strict)

End your response with a fenced ```json``` block matching this schema:

```json
{
  "new_features": [
    {
      "title": "≤80 char title",
      "description": "≤500 char description, why + what + acceptance criteria",
      "type": "feature|bug|optimization",
      "priority": "P0|P1|P2|P3",
      "parent_goal": "{{ goal.name }}"
    }
  ],
  "skipped_goals": [
    {"name": "{{ goal.name }}", "reason": "<short>"}
  ]
}
```

Rules:

- **Maximum {{ max_features }} features** per goal per round.
- Each feature must be independently actionable (don't bundle multiple ideas).
- Skip the goal entirely (`new_features: []`, populate `skipped_goals`) if its
  KPIs are already met or there's a closely related open feature in flight.
